te.cpp:95:3\r\n2412 | [ts-3] | #1 0x7f8d5cad6a4c in yb::tserver::RemoteBootstrapAnchorClient::KeepLogAnchorAliveAsync() ${BUILD_ROOT}/../../src/yb/tserver/remote_bootstrap_anchor_client.cc:140:40\r\n2413 | [ts-3] | #2 0x7f8d5cb2db48 in yb::tserver::RemoteBootstrapSession::RefreshRemoteLogAnchorSessionAsync() ${BUILD_ROOT}/../../src/yb/tserver/remote_bootstrap_session.cc:555:5\r\n2414 | [ts-3] | #3 0x7f8d5cb0f709 in yb::tserver::RemoteBootstrapServiceImpl::SessionData::ResetExpiration(yb::tserver::RemoteBootstrapErrorPB_Code*) ${BUILD_ROOT}/../../src/yb/tserver/remote_bootstrap_service.cc:429:26\r\n```\r\n\r\nSeems like a pretty obvious leak, where we new a response, but there's no smart pointers around it's ownership to delete the memory. cc @amitanandaiyer @rthallamko3 \r\n\r\nThis seems like a product leak too! Release wise, this is in 2.16.\r\n\r\n[DB-5454]: https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-5454?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ","closed_by":{"login":"basavaraj29","id":17742021,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzQyMDIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17742021?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/basavaraj29","html_url":"https://github.com/basavaraj29","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basavaraj29/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basavaraj29/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basavaraj29/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basavaraj29/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basavaraj29/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basavaraj29/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basavaraj29/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basavaraj29/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basavaraj29/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"rea